```.t {tagname} <effect> <effect args> <subcommand> <subcommand args>```
Note: Put the effect in quotation marks "like this"
VERY IMPORTANT NOTE: Put all required effect arguments before your subcommand
## Sub-Command List ##
-# These are optional and not required
`raw <medianame> <oldpitchsystem?>` - Shows the raw iscript code for an effect
`ihtx <powers> <nosnip?> <notrim?> <oldpitchsystem?>` - Does an IHTX with the effect for a set amount of powers, may end up frying Avocado's computer
`raw ihtx <powers> <nosnip?> <notrim?> <oldpitchsystem?>` - A combination of the previous two
`multiplier <powers> <oldpitchsystem?>` - Does an effect on the source for a set amount of powers
`ihtxbuggy` - Adds an offset for each export
`ihtxold` - Brings back the meme text from the old versions of my ihtx tags
`ihtxkine` - Adds a Fade In/Out effect, similar to Kinemaster
`oldpitch` - Adds the old pitch system back without having to use the `ihtx` commands
## Non-Effect Command List ##
-# These commands do not work with effects, so just do ".t {tagname} <command>", don't add any effects
`list` - Shows a BIG list of effects (planning to convert it to an embed)
`updatelog` - Shows the new update log!
